<p class="copy">
	Little used in true naval warfare, the fighters of 2200 act most often as escort or scout craft. Fighters have little impact in fleet engagements, where the much heavier vessels of a navy battlegroup can make short work of them. Instead, they are used as combat craft against threats that don't warrant the attention of an actual warship. Featuring a crew of one to three and systems for unmanned operation, fighters provide a relatively inexpensive military presence in far-flung systems.
</p>
<p class="copy">
	Too small to mount <?php echo sf_lore_link('aether-sails', 'aether sails'); ?> or the <?php echo sf_lore_link('switch-gates', 'Switch Gates'); ?> used to refuel their thrusters, these craft are often locked to the hull of a larger ship until needed. Indeed, many a <?php echo sf_lore_link('freighters', 'freighter'); ?> has seen off a pirate attack with the quick launch of a few fighters tucked into its berth.
</p>
